From b39da5d7daffd1362270b7580af1b449cbc05bcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangyicong <wangyicong@bytedance.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:12:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sm90): preserve MegaMoE on DeepGEMM 2.8

Port onto the vLLM v0.32.0 DeepGEMM pin 1e1842a83, retaining the
release Torch operator registration and Python native-library facade.
Original optimization: 72586051f9d78e16fcd26af13bdcef1a74ac610f.
SM90 source snapshot: 45a95bac4d70abf3a66780922ee65ca0cdaddc3b.

Restore the tuned SS FP8xFP4 and FP8 paths, compact SM90 workspace,
legacy wave scheduler, FP32 activation scales, GS32 weight packer,
pre-dispatch and per-call SM budgets. Flatten tuple arguments at the
Torch boundary and serialize buffer-slicing geometry instead of exporting
a pybind closure. Preserve the release SM100 scheduler and dependency pins.
Native build and GPU validation remain required before accepting this port.
The final independent RS/backend update is carried in a following commit.

Original commit description:

Restore and adapt the SM90 MegaMoE API, heuristics, and JIT sources on top of the DeepGEMM 2.8/DeepJIT baseline.

Co-authored-by: TRAE (GPT-6) <traecli@bytedance.com>
Signed-off-by: trae-solo-agent <solo-agent@trae.ai>
